WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.451
Wiring it into CI.

2
00:00:01.731 --> 00:00:05.187
In GitHub Actions, the tiers map onto workflow triggers.

3
00:00:05.467 --> 00:00:13.509
A pull_request trigger with a paths filter runs the live smoke set only when prompts, model config, or the eval itself change.

4
00:00:13.789 --> 00:00:21.661
A schedule trigger with a cron expression runs the nightly suite, and workflow_dispatch lets someone run it by hand before a release.

5
00:00:21.941 --> 00:00:24.779
Three details from GitHub’s docs are worth knowing.

6
00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:32.717
Cron schedules run in UTC unless you set a time zone, and they run only on the latest commit of the default branch.

7
00:00:32.997 --> 00:00:38.907
Scheduled runs can be delayed at busy times, especially the top of the hour, so pick an odd minute.

8
00:00:39.187 --> 00:00:51.091
And in public repositories, scheduled workflows are disabled automatically after 60 days without repository activity, which can silently stop a nightly eval on a quiet project.

9
00:00:51.371 --> 00:00:56.448
API keys go in the repository’s encrypted secrets, never in the workflow file.

10
00:00:56.728 --> 00:01:02.573
Upload the results file and manifest as a build artifact so anyone can rerun the analysis.

11
00:01:02.853 --> 00:01:10.939
The lab for this week includes a complete example workflow that runs the offline gate; it sits in the lab folder rather than in.

12
00:01:11.219 --> 00:01:16.552
github/workflows, so it documents the pattern without running on this repository.
